        "original_id": "cd749e91-8872-51da-9bde-452b056b11c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gülhane Park, Eminönü, Istanbul, Turkey\n- Organizations: Zografeion Lyceum\n- Systems: Topkapı Palace\n- Topics: Greek schools in Istanbul\n\nFacts:\n- Gülhane Park is a historical urban park in the Eminönü district of Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Gülhane Park is located adjacent to and on the grounds of Topkapı Palace.\n- The name Gülhane Park derives from the Persian “Gulkhāna,” meaning “house of flowers,” and the Turkish name “Gülhane Parkı” means “Rosehouse Park.”\n- Zografeion Lyceum is one of the remaining open Greek schools in Istanbul.\n- Zografeion Lyceum is known in Turkish as “Özel Zoğrafyon Rum Lisesi” and in Greek as “Ζωγράφειον Λύκειον.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
